 "name": "wpthb: a phase-shifted full bridge driving a wireless-power link",
 "description": "The 24 V full bridge of the wpthb board (Q1 to Q4 on VHB, its tank C25/C27/C30 and the primary coil on TP15/TP14), the input filter (R9, CA1 to CA4, L3) and a receiver: a coil like the primary, a series capacitor and a load. Leg B's phase is set so the load takes P. Secondary is assumed identical to the primary, not supplied receiver hardware. Target receiver power is obtained by adjusting phase at 24 V, not by imposing a fixed power sink. Switch and passive parasitics are editable engineering placeholders, not extracted manufacturer values. Coil core conductance is fitted to small-signal Q=155 at 125 kHz and held constant; broadband/large-signal/temperature behavior is not measured. Input filter is electrical; upstream copper, coil geometry, gate circuitry and environment coupling are not field-modeled. The receiver's capacitor and load are fixed: tuned and matched at 90 kHz.",
